-- ── Decision refinements DISCOVERED during the round (recorded honestly;
--    each is an interpretation the pre-registration did not fully pin) ──
-- D10a (NEW): scope.predicate = None (§5.5 «все предикаты автора») enumerates
--   the author's DATA facts and EXCLUDES the reserved supersedes ledger.
--   Discovered by the battery: a repeated All-scope supersede would otherwise
--   kill the author's own PRIOR supersessions and resurrect the very facts it
--   retracted (oscillation — observed live as a red test before the fix).
--   The §2.4 recursion stays fully expressible by NAMING the predicate
--   (predicate: Some(supersedes)) — exactly what the resurrection test does.
-- D12a (NEW, forced by contract (2)): the direct-assert boundary ALSO enforces
--   §4.2 — a Supersedes group whose victim aid belongs to a FOREIGN author is
--   E-SUP-001; without it, FactGroup::Supersedes would have been an author-
--   scope bypass. assertion_ticks_snapshot resolves aid → (tick, author) over
--   the raw (dead-inclusive) assertion set: re-superseding a dead own aid is
--   legal; an unresolvable aid is E-SUP-001.
-- D2-as-implemented: the c0 of a scope-kill supersedes fact is
--   aid(aid_old, author, at_tick) — PER-VICTIM (not per-operation), reusing
--   the aid combinator; pre-registered in D2, confirmed. Liveness only ever
--   consults c1 (verified by the recursion test).
-- Empty-victim supersede: a scope matching nothing commits nothing and
--   returns the current version token (mirror of the empty assert_batch).
-- Corrupt reserved records (unparseable aid_new/aid_old or record-id ≠ tuple
--   fid): contractual panic carrying E-SUP-001 — corruption of the truth
--   source, same channel class as D3.

