-- ── Review-round resolutions (finalize, R6 repairs-as-repairs) ─────
-- F1 (minor, FIXED): post_supersession_reads_and_legacy_visibility's final
--   post-compaction check discarded live_multiset results while the comment
--   claimed read stability. Repaired per the reviewer's suggested fix: the
--   four per-predicate live multisets (node/edge/attr/supersedes) are now
--   captured BEFORE FullMerge and assert_multiset_eq'd after — the claim is
--   asserted, not implied via the sha equality alone.
-- F2 (minor, RECORDED — no P4 change): FactStore::stats() is OnceLock-
--   memoized per store instance (lsm.rs get_or_init, pre-existing P3
--   behavior, identical at HEAD d4695275) with no invalidation on
--   assert_batch/supersede; P4 makes the counts newly MUTABLE via
--   supersession, so a long-lived store's planner stats can go stale.
--   Pre-registered as C20 once-semantics; carried forward as a REQUIRED item
--   for the P6/P7 wiring round: invalidate or version the stats cache on
--   commit/supersede (e.g. key by manifest version) BEFORE the derive
--   executor consumes stats(supersedes) from a long-lived store.
-- F3 (minor, process note): a concurrent reviewer session ran cargo jobs on
--   the shared worktree during the test window; timed perf runs were
--   protected by explicit quiescence checks and all medians passed with >8%
--   margin (no contamination). Process rule going forward: serialize
--   reviewer cargo invocations against the test-runner's timed-perf window
--   (extends the R6 no-stash rule to builds during timing), and use a
--   self-excluding quiescence probe — pgrep -fa 'rustup.*(cargo|rustc)' —
--   because pgrep -f 'cargo (test|build)|rustc' self-matches its own bash
--   wrapper and naive loops spin forever.
